{title: I Know Who Holds Tomorrow}
{key: G}

{comment: Intro}
[G]     [C]     [D]     [G]

{comment: Verse 1}
I don't [G]know about to[G7]morrow;
I just [C]live from day to [G]day.
I don't [C]borrow from its [G]sunshine
For its [A7]skies may turn to [D]grey.
I don't [G]worry o'er the [G7]future,
For I [C]know what Jesus [G]said.
And to[C]day I'll walk be[G]side Him,
For He [G]knows[D] what is a[G]head.

{comment: Chorus}
Many [C]things about to[G]morrow
I don't [A7]seem to unders[D]tand
But I [G]know who holds to[C]morrow
And I [G]know [D]who holds my [G]hand.

{comment: Verse 2}
Every [G]step is getting [G7]brighter
As the [C]golden stairs I [G]climb;
Every [C]burden's getting [G]lighter,
Every [A7]cloud is silver-[D]lined.
There the [G]sun is always [G7]shining,
There no [C]tear will dim the [G]eye;
At the [C]ending of the [G]rainbow
Where the [G]mounta[D]ins touch the [G]sky.

{comment: Verse 3}
I don't [G]know about [G7]tomorrow;
It may [C]bring me pover[G]ty.
But the [C]one who feeds the s[G]parrow,
Is the [A7]one who stands by [D]me.
And the [G]path that is my [G7]portion
May be [C]through the flame or [G]flood;
But His [C]presence goes be[G]fore me
And I'm [G]cover[D]ed with His [G]blood.
